---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";

const lastUpdated = "September 2026";
---
<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy — Lead From The Hip"
	description="What this site collects, what it doesn't, and what happens to your data if you book a call or subscribe to the Substack."
>
	<Hero
		eyebrow="Privacy"
		standfirst="Short version: this site doesn't collect much. Here's the specific version."
	>
		What this site does <span class="accent">with your data.</span>
	</Hero>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">What this site collects</h2>
		<p class="text-ink measure">
			Nothing, directly. There's no analytics, no tracking pixels, no
			cookies, and no forms on this site. There's nothing here to opt out
			of, because nothing is being gathered in the first place.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">If you book a call</h2>
		<p class="text-ink measure">
			The "Book a call" button hands you off to Calendly. Whatever you
			enter there — name, email, whatever you write in the notes — is
			collected and handled by Calendly, not by this site. Their policy is
			at{" "}
			<a
				href="https://calendly.com/privacy"
				class="text-petrol underline hover:opacity-80 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-petrol"
			>
				calendly.com/privacy
			</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">If you follow the Substack</h2>
		<p class="text-ink measure">
			Following or subscribing happens on Substack's platform. They collect
			your email to deliver posts, and that relationship is governed by
			their policy, not this site's — at{" "}
			<a
				href="https://substack.com/privacy"
				class="text-petrol underline hover:opacity-80 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-petrol"
			>
				substack.com/privacy
			</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">Changes</h2>
		<p class="text-ink measure">
			If that ever changes — an analytics tool, a contact form, anything
			that collects something new — this page gets updated first, and
			gets specific about what and why.
		</p>
		<p class="text-muted text-sm mt-4">Last updated: {lastUpdated}.</p>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
